  "worked_solution": "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $E$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(E)=4\\cdot 7-8\\cdot 3=4\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(E)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E{E}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,\u2713 \\\\ {E}^{-1}E & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
